disable systemd-sysext.service
disable systemd-sysext.socket
disable systemd-confext.service
disable systemd-confext.socket

# Boot does not wait for the network. systemd enables wait-online with networkd
# (90-systemd.preset, and networkd.service Also=), so any unit that pulls
# network-online.target held boot up to 120 s, then failed the unit, on a
# device with no link. Without it network-online.target is a plain
# synchronization point. A product that needs a link before a service starts
# enables systemd-networkd-wait-online.service by shipping the wants link in
# an extension overlay:
#   overlay/etc/systemd/system/network-online.target.wants/systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
#     -> /usr/lib/systemd/system/systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
# enable_services can't (the unit is in the base rootfs, not the extension's
# sysroot), a preset can't (this file is matched first, and preset lookup stops
# at the first match), and RequiredForOnline= only picks the links it waits for
# once enabled. wait-online-any.conf then applies.
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
